 {"id":"fabro-11d3","title":"Planner tie-break: prefer seeds closing an observed failure class over same-priority polish","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T19:28:38.815Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T19:38:45.157Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md step 2, add a tie-break line: prefer seeds that close a failure class observed in recent runs (e.g. fabro-9372 current_seed_id projection, fabro-6b58 in-flight bound) over same-priority polish seeds. In the basis run two polish seeds were claimed while those prevention seeds sat open and the duplicate-claim race recurred, costing 12 minutes and a manual halt. Basis: run 01M23RQRCB748R4VRXA2WE6BZ0, workflow version 3b17faf145735aa14caf619a38c0b079a1ff1c91acf24211c9ab08a2612c6f6f, commit d55d6ea53c41f53c116ba063221f2988223072dd","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-55a7","title":"Planner: batch reconnaissance into one shell call (sd ready + sd show + base-branch grep)","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T19:28:38.909Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T19:38:45.247Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md, batch reconnaissance into a single shell call instead of many tool calls. In the basis run the two planner passes spent 92.0 s and 93.5 s inference over 8 separate calls each; the in-flight check alone took 3 round-trips. Expected ~40-60 s and ~$0.06 saved per pass (36% of run cost was planner), and a shorter claim-to-dispatch window (21 s here) narrows the duplicate-claim race. Basis: run 01M23RQRCB748R4VRXA2WE6BZ0, workflow version 3b17faf145735aa14caf619a38c0b079a1ff1c91acf24211c9ab08a2612c6f6f, commit d55d6ea53c41f53c116ba063221f2988223072dd","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-c080","title":"Engine: re-resolve stage prompt files from the run branch tip so self-referential seeds don't review under stale prompts","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T19:47:40.170Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T19:52:24.377Z","description":"Run 01M23TE61D4Y33415BK5M7C70X: the deliverable added an adjudication line to reviewer.md, but the reviewer's injected prompt was the pre-change snapshot materialized at run creation; it judged correctly only because it happened to cross-check the on-disk file (journal observation 3, seq 288). Change: engine run-spec resolution — re-resolve prompt files from the run branch tip at stage start, or at minimum append a 'this run modified your prompt — judge the on-disk version, diff in evidence' notice; same mechanism fabro-dc81 requests for [run.pull_request] in lib/components/fabro-workflow/src/pipeline/publish.rs. Effect: prompt-editing seeds (half the backlog) can never silently review against superseded instructions. Basis: run 01M23TE61D4Y33415BK5M7C70X, workflow version c25ec2416a5e45108d80b6ea43ca9f9e394a3f8fab9ed6d0e53cfa2d3e45bdfa, commit 592f64bd92615069d6a7dbf32cc98c75eabb74e6","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
-{"id":"fabro-bfe1","title":"Qualitygate: add a loop-asset tier with a checked-in evidence-smoke.nu regression","status":"in_progress","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T19:47:40.355Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T20:01:51.980Z","description":"Run 01M23TE61D4Y33415BK5M7C70X: the tester's 'just qualitygate' ran 4.15s with 'no crates touched / format clean' — zero machine verification of the actual changes (evidence.nu, reviewer.md). Verification fell to the two costliest LLM stages: implementer hand-built a scratch-git exercise (216s inference) and the reviewer re-ran it (57s), then the regression exercise was deleted at closeout. Change: in the qualitygate recipe (justfile / scripts/qualitygate.nu) add a loop-asset tier — a 'nu -c source' check for .fabro/workflows/develop/scripts/*.nu plus a checked-in mixed-capture scratch exercise as evidence-smoke.nu following the existing closeout-smoke.nu pattern. Effect: deterministic verification of loop-asset changes, durable regression coverage, fewer manual-verification turns. Distinct from fabro-50f8 (prompt-mandated ad-hoc exercises) and fabro-574d (crate derivation): gate infrastructure plus a durable checked-in regression. Basis: run 01M23TE61D4Y33415BK5M7C70X, workflow version c25ec2416a5e45108d80b6ea43ca9f9e394a3f8fab9ed6d0e53cfa2d3e45bdfa, commit 592f64bd92615069d6a7dbf32cc98c75eabb74e6","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
